# Installation

Three steps: point Composer at the repositories, require the pack, seed it.

## Requirements

PHP `^8.4.1 || ^8.5`, Laravel `^13`, and [`ichava/core`](https://github.com/ichava/core) on the same application. Core is
the engine; this pack is only icons and the provider that registers them. The authoritative
constraint is in `composer.json`.

## The repositories block

Nothing in this ecosystem is published to Packagist, so Composer has to be told where to look.
Composer reads `repositories` only from the root package, which is why the block belongs in the
**application's** `composer.json` and names the whole transitive closure rather than just this pack.
Core's [installation guide](https://github.com/ichava/core/blob/main/docs/installation.md) gives the full block.

## Require it

```bash
composer require {{packageName}}
```

The service provider is discovered automatically.

## Seed it

```bash
php artisan ichava::ichava-core.database seed --package={{packageName}}
```

**This step is not optional.** Until it runs the registry holds no rows for this pack and every
lookup returns nothing. See [seed pack icons](https://github.com/ichava/core/blob/main/docs/recipes/seed-pack-icons.md).

## No configuration to publish

The pack ships no config file and no publish tag; its settings live in
`resources/assets/svg/config.json`. See [Configuration](configuration.md).

